 66   40C8              ; scan: B rows of the keyboard, from row 0, into the bytes from HL; a bit at 0
 67   40C8              ; is a key held down. Port C's top four bits drive the cassette motor and its
 68   40C8              ; output, the CAPS lamp and the click (chapter 3): they go back as they were.
 69   40C8              ; The interrupts must be off. Uses A, B, C, HL
 70   40C8 DB AA        scan:   in a, (PPI_C)           ; 12
